render_lab's runtime library for Lamlet
=======================================

A package's scripts (its `script/…` resources, lab/src/script/runtime.rs) are Lamlet that the lab runs while the
viewer plays and while a video records: what the investigation's native code computes stays native (its passes,
its CPU mirrors, a ray through the scene), and the scripts say what to do with it (where an overlay's arrows go,
what a click sets, how a value moves over time). Every script imports this package as
`$$[Import* render_lab_runtime]`; it is the same for every investigation.

A script keeps nothing between calls. Each hook is a function of what the lab passes in (the frame's time, a
click, an action's arguments) and of what it reads (the shot's values, through the investigation's values
package `<package>_values`, and the natives), and returns a description: shapes to draw, or values to set, which
the lab checks and applies after the call returns.

$[Import* std]$[ImportAs rl_runtime rt]

Types

A point or a direction in the scene, in metres; and the two- and four-component vectors values hold.
$[# Vec3 [% {Struct {' {Field "x" Float} {Field "y" Float} {Field "z" Float}}}]]
$[# Vec2 [% {Struct {' {Field "x" Float} {Field "y" Float}}}]]
$[# Vec4 [% {Struct {' {Field "x" Float} {Field "y" Float} {Field "z" Float} {Field "w" Float}}}]]

A value a hook sets: a key of the shot (lab/src/values.rs) and its value. The values package's setters
(`setVectorsShown 1.0`) make them; the lab checks every one (the key, its type, an integer's range) before it
applies any, in order.
$[# Write [% {Struct {' {Field "key" String} {Field "value" Data}}}]]

$[# _Segment [% {Struct {'
    {Field "from" Vec3}
    {Field "to" Vec3}
    {Field "color" String}
    {Field "alpha" Float}
    {Field "width" Float}
    {Field "arrow" Bool}
    {Field "dashed" Bool}}}]]
$[# _Point [% {Struct {'
    {Field "at" Vec3}
    {Field "radius" Float}
    {Field "color" String}
    {Field "alpha" Float}}}]]
$[# _Label [% {Struct {' {Field "at" Vec3} {Field "text" String} {Field "color" String}}}]]

What an overlay draws over the scene (lab/src/frame.rs `DrawLists`, `Label`): a segment (an arrow, or dashed), a
point, or a label beside a point, whose text is written out (`label`) or a key of the package's text table
(`labelText`). A colour is `#rrggbb`, or one of the theme's, which follow the viewer's theme: `textColor`,
`textDimColor`, `textFaintColor`, `accentColor`. Nothing with an alpha of 0 or less is drawn.
$[# Shape [% {Variant {'
    {Field "segment" _Segment}
    {Field "point" _Point}
    {Field "label" _Label}
    {Field "labelText" _Label}}}]]

A row of the readout beside the scene (lab/src/frame.rs `Readout`): its name, its value, and the value's colour
(as a shape's).
$[# Row [% {Struct {' {Field "name" String} {Field "value" String} {Field "color" String}}}]]

A click on an image or the scene: the point clicked, 0 to 1 across and down.
$[# Click [% {Struct {' {Field "u" Float} {Field "v" Float}}}]]

The hooks the lab finds in a package's scripts by their types (a binding whose name starts with `_` is never
one):

- an overlay, `Overlay`, the shapes drawn over each frame at its time in seconds;
- a readout, `Readout`, rows added to the frame's readout (after the investigation's own), at its time;
- a click handler, `ClickHandler`, named by its binding as a `#[click]` handler is (`imageClick`);
- an action, `{Action Args}`, which a story runs (`{run "name"}`) with its arguments as the record `Args`, at the
  seconds since the story started it;
- an animation, `Animation`, the values at a demonstration's time in seconds (its `animation` in the demo's
  TOML).

A hook's type must be exactly one of these: ascribe it (`{: {^ {t} …} Overlay}`). A script's function that returns
what a hook returns but takes something else, or that is generic, fails the script; a helper's name starts with `_`.
$[# Overlay [% {Fn {' Float} {List Shape}}]]
$[# Readout [% {Fn {' Float} {List Row}}]]
$[# ClickHandler [% {Fn {' Click} {List Write}}]]
$[# Animation [% {Fn {' Float} {List Write}}]]
$[# {Action args} {Fn {' Float args} {List Write}}]

The shot

Fn([], String). The key of the demonstration the shot shows (`ibl`).
$[# {demo} {rt::demo}]

Fn([String], String). The package's text `key` (`textKey`) in the viewer's language, or the lab's.
$[# {text key} {rt::text key}]

Vectors

Fn([Float, Float, Float], Vec3). A vector.
$[# {vec3 x y z} {: {. x x y y z z} Vec3}]
Fn([Vec3, Vec3], Vec3). The sum.
$[# {vadd a b} {vec3 {+ {.x a} {.x b}} {+ {.y a} {.y b}} {+ {.z a} {.z b}}}]
Fn([Vec3, Vec3], Vec3). The difference.
$[# {vsub a b} {vec3 {- {.x a} {.x b}} {- {.y a} {.y b}} {- {.z a} {.z b}}}]
Fn([Vec3, Float], Vec3). Scaled by `s`.
$[# {vscale a s} {vec3 {* {.x a} s} {* {.y a} s} {* {.z a} s}}]
Fn([Vec3, Vec3], Float). The dot product.
$[# {vdot a b} {+ {+ {* {.x a} {.x b}} {* {.y a} {.y b}}} {* {.z a} {.z b}}}]
Fn([Vec3, Vec3], Vec3). The cross product.
$[# {vcross a b} {vec3
    {- {* {.y a} {.z b}} {* {.z a} {.y b}}}
    {- {* {.z a} {.x b}} {* {.x a} {.z b}}}
    {- {* {.x a} {.y b}} {* {.y a} {.x b}}}}]
Fn([Vec3], Float). The length.
$[# {vlength a} {sqrt {vdot a a}}]
Fn([Vec3], Vec3). The unit vector along `a`.
$[# {vnormalize a} {vscale a {/ 1.0 {vlength a}}}]

Fn([Vec3], Vec3). A unit vector perpendicular to the unit vector `n` (Duff et al. 2017, "Building an
Orthonormal Basis, Revisited", as glam's `any_orthonormal_vector`).
$[# {anyOrthonormal n}
    [# sign {!if {< {.z n} 0.0} -1.0 1.0}]
    [# a {/ -1.0 {+ sign {.z n}}}]
    {vec3 {* {* {.x n} {.y n}} a} {+ sign {* {* {.y n} {.y n}} a}} {neg {.y n}}}]

Fn([Vec3, Vec3], Vec3). The direction perpendicular to `n` in the plane of `n` and `l`, or any perpendicular one
when `l` is along `n`.
$[# {inPlane n l}
    [# t {vsub l {vscale n {vdot n l}}}]
    {!if {> {vdot t t} 0.000001} {vnormalize t} {anyOrthonormal n}}]

Fn([Vec3, Vec3], Vec3). The mirror direction of `l` about the normal `n`.
$[# {mirror n l} {vnormalize {vsub {vscale n {* 2.0 {vdot n l}}} l}}]

Fn([Vec3, Vec3, Int], List(Vec3)). `count + 1` directions swept from horizon to horizon through `n`, in the
plane of `n` and its perpendicular `t`.
$[# {sweep n t count} {map
    {range 0 {+ count 1}}
    {^ {k}
        [# a {* {- {/ {float k} {float count}} 0.5} pi}]
        {vadd {vscale n {cos a}} {vscale t {sin a}}}}}]

Easings and curves

A curve is a function of time, `Fn([Float], Float)`: an animation is the values its curves give at the
demonstration's time, an action's at the seconds since the story started it. Nothing remembers where a value
was; a sequence is a function of time too (`seq`).

The lab's eases (lab/src/animation.rs `Ease`), each from 0 to 1 over 0 to 1.

Fn([Float], Float). Smootherstep: at rest at both ends (the lab's `smooth`).
$[# {smooth x} {* {* {* x x} x} {+ {* x {- {* x 6.0} 15.0}} 10.0}}]
Fn([Float], Float). Constant speed.
$[# {linear x} x]
Fn([Float], Float). Cubic, from rest.
$[# {easeIn x} {* {* x x} x}]
Fn([Float], Float). Cubic, to rest.
$[# {easeOut x} [# y {- 1.0 x}] {- 1.0 {* {* y y} y}}]
Fn([Float], Float). Cubic, at rest at both ends.
$[# {easeInOut x}
    [# y {- 1.0 x}]
    {!if {< x 0.5} {* 4.0 {* {* x x} x}} {- 1.0 {* 4.0 {* {* y y} y}}}}]
Fn([Float], Float). Half a cosine: a ping-pong of it is a pure sine.
$[# {easeSine x} {- 0.5 {* 0.5 {cos {* pi x}}}}]

Fn([Float, Float], Float). The fraction of `seconds` done `t` seconds in, held at 0 before and 1 after.
$[# {once seconds t} {clamp {/ t seconds} 0.0 1.0}]
Fn([Float, Float], Float). The fraction of `seconds` done, starting again every `seconds`.
$[# {looping seconds t} [# x {/ t seconds}] {- x {float {floor x}}}]
Fn([Float, Float], Float). The fraction of `seconds` done, running back to 0 and forward again.
$[# {pingPong seconds t}
    [# x {/ t seconds}]
    {- 1.0 {abs {- {- x {* 2.0 {float {floor {/ x 2.0}}}}} 1.0}}}]
Fn([Float, Float], Int). How many whole steps of `seconds` are done `t` seconds in. A step counts from the frame it
starts on: `t` comes from whole frames, so a quotient a rounding short of a whole number (4 × 0.7 s is
2.8 s, but 2.8 / 0.7 is 3.9999999999999996) is that number.
$[# {steps seconds t} {floor {+ {/ t seconds} 0.0001}}]
Fn([Float, Float, Fn([Float], Float), Float], Float). From `from` to `to`, eased, at the fraction `x`.
$[# {tween from to ease x} {lerp from to {ease x}}]

Fn([Float, Float, Float, Float], Float). A sine wave around `center`, `amplitude` high, every `period` seconds
(the lab's `Wave`: `center + amplitude · sin(2π t / period)`).
$[# {wave center amplitude period t} {+ center {* amplitude {sin {/ {* {* 2.0 pi} t} period}}}}]
Fn([Float, Float, Float, Float], Float). The same wave a quarter period earlier, a cosine.
$[# {cosineWave center amplitude period t} {+ center {* amplitude {sin {+
    {/ {* {* 2.0 pi} t} period}
    {/ pi 2.0}}}}}]

$[# _Span [% {Struct {' {Field "seconds" Float} {Field "curve" {Fn {' Float} Float}}}}]]

Fn([Float, Fn([Float], Float)], {curve: Fn([Float], Float), seconds: Float}). A part of a sequence: a curve
for `seconds`, given the seconds since its part began.
$[# {span seconds curve} {: {. seconds seconds curve curve} _Span}]

Fn([List({curve: Fn([Float], Float), seconds: Float}), Float], Float). Parts one after another (at least one):
at `t`, the part that holds `t`, at the seconds since it began; the last part holds its end after it.
$[# {seq spans t}
    [# {_at rest start}
        [# s {head rest}]
        [# local {- t start}]
        {!if {!or {isEmpty {tail rest}} {< local {.seconds s}}}
            {{.curve s} {clamp local 0.0 {.seconds s}}}
            {_at {tail rest} {+ start {.seconds s}}}}]
    {_at spans 0.0}]

Shapes

Fn([Vec3, Vec3, String, Float, Float], Shape). A segment, `width` pixels wide.
$[# {segment from to color alpha width} {: {#segment {.
    from from
    to to
    color color
    alpha alpha
    width width
    arrow false
    dashed false}} Shape}]
Fn([Vec3, Vec3, String, Float, Float], Shape). An arrow from `from` to `to`.
$[# {arrow from to color alpha width} {: {#segment {.
    from from
    to to
    color color
    alpha alpha
    width width
    arrow true
    dashed false}} Shape}]
Fn([Vec3, Vec3, String, Float, Float], Shape). A dashed segment.
$[# {dashed from to color alpha width} {: {#segment {.
    from from
    to to
    color color
    alpha alpha
    width width
    arrow false
    dashed true}} Shape}]
Fn([Vec3, Float, String, Float], Shape). A point, `radius` pixels across.
$[# {point at radius color alpha} {: {#point {.
    at at
    radius radius
    color color
    alpha alpha}} Shape}]
Fn([Vec3, String, String], Shape). A label beside `at`, its text as written (a symbol: `N`).
$[# {label at text color} {: {#label {. at at text text color color}} Shape}]
Fn([Vec3, String, String], Shape). A label beside `at`, its text the package's text `key` (`textKey`).
$[# {labelText at key color} {: {#labelText {. at at text key color color}} Shape}]
Fn([String], String). A key of the package's text table, as `labelText` takes it; the text check
(lab/check) finds the keys a script names this way.
$[# {textKey key} key]

Fn([String, String, String], Row). A readout row.
$[# {row name value color} {: {. name name value value color color} Row}]

Fn([Int], String). A whole number 0 or more in hexadecimal, upper case, at least two digits (`1F`).
$[# _hexDigits [% {chars "0123456789ABCDEF"}]]
$[# {_hex n} {!if {< n 16} {nth _hexDigits n} {++ {_hex {div n 16}} {nth _hexDigits {% n 16}}}}]
$[# {hex2 n} [# h {_hex n}] {!if {< n 16} {++ "0" h} h}]

Fn([Vec3, Int], String). A vector as `(x, y, z)`, each with `digits` decimals.
$[# {vectorText v digits}
    f"{(${fixed {.x v} digits}, ${fixed {.y v} digits}, ${fixed {.z v} digits})}"]

Fn([List(Vec3), String, Float, Float], List(Shape)). Segments through the points in turn.
$[# {polyline points color alpha width} {!if {isEmpty points}
    {'}
    {map {zip points {tail points}} {^ {p} {segment {.first p} {.second p} color alpha width}}}}]

$[# _Arrow [% {Struct {' {Field "name" String} {Field "dir" Vec3} {Field "color" String}}}]]

Fn([String, Vec3, String], {color: String, dir: Vec3, name: String}). One of `grownArrows`'s arrows: its name,
its direction (a unit vector), and its colour.
$[# {named name dir color} {: {. name name dir dir color color} _Arrow}]

Fn([Vec3, List({color: String, dir: Vec3, name: String}), Float, Float, Float, Float], List(Shape)). Arrows
`size` long from `at`, each labelled with its name, the first `count` of them: a fractional count grows the next one
out of the point (smoothly), and its label shows once it is past 0.6 of its length.
$[# {grownArrows at arrows size alpha width count} {flatten {map
    {zip {range 0 {length arrows}} arrows}
    {^ {e}
        [# i {float {.first e}}]
        [# a {.second e}]
        [# grown {!if {>= count {+ i 1.0}} 1.0 {smooth {- count i}}}]
        [# tip {vadd at {vscale {.dir a} {* size grown}}}]
        [# shaft {' {arrow at tip {.color a} alpha width}}]
        [# name {!if {> grown 0.6}
            {' {label {vadd at {vscale {.dir a} {+ {* size grown} 0.04}}} {.name a} {.color a}}}
            {'}}]
        {!if {> count i} {append shaft name} {'}}}}}]

Fn([List(Float)], Float). The largest value, or 0 when none is above 0.
$[# {_peak values} {fold values 0.0 max}]

Fn([List(Vec3), List(Float)], Vec3). The direction of the largest value (the last of equal ones).
$[# {_tip dirs values} {.first {fold
    {tail {zip dirs values}}
    {head {zip dirs values}}
    {^ {best e} {!if {>= {.second e} {.second best}} e best}}}}]

Fn([Vec3, List(Vec3), List(Float), String, Float, Float, Float, Option(String)], List(Shape)). A polar plot
around `at`: each value as a radius along its direction, scaled so the largest is `size`, closed through `at`;
with a text key, labelled at its tip. Nothing when no value is above 0.
$[# {lobeLine at dirs values color size alpha width tag}
    [# peak {_peak values}]
    [# {line u}
        [# points {append
            {cons at {map
                {zip dirs values}
                {^ {e} {vadd at {vscale {.first e} {/ {* size {.second e}} peak}}}}}}
            {' at}}]
        {polyline points color alpha width}]
    [# {_labelled u} {caseOption tag
        {^ {} {'}}
        {^ {key} {' {labelText {vadd at {vscale {_tip dirs values} {+ size 0.06}}} key color}}}}]
    {!if {<= peak 0.0} {'} {append {line unit} {_labelled unit}}}]

Colours

The lab's palette (lab/src/palette.rs): the normal, the direction to the viewer, a reflected ray, an incident
one, and what is selected.
$[# normalColor "#6be3b0"]
$[# viewColor "#8fb8ff"]
$[# reflectedColor "#ff6fb5"]
$[# incidentColor "#ffa14a"]
$[# selectedColor "#ffd166"]

The theme's text colours (full, dim, faint) and its accent, as the viewer's theme draws them.
$[# textColor "text"]
$[# textDimColor "textDim"]
$[# textFaintColor "textFaint"]
$[# accentColor "accent"]
